<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Strata Florida Abbey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1164</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Strata <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> Abbey is a ruined Cistercian abbey near Pontrhydfendigaid in Ceredigion, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, founded in 1164 and soon refounded on its present site under the patronage of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhys-ap-gruffydd">Rhys ap Gruffydd</a>. It became a centre of Welsh learning and politics, where chronicles of the Welsh princes were probably kept, and a burial place of the princes of Deheubarth. It was dissolved in 1539.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/strata-florida-abbey.jpg" alt="Strata Florida Abbey" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: By William M. Connolley. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DSCN4297-strata-florida-arch.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
